  "id": "COMPOUND:26432 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Echitamidine is implicated in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota through a multi-step pathway involving multiple targets. The evidence suggests that Echitamidine acts as a target for CX-1 and LAMA-84, which in turn are targets of Neocurcumenol and methyl (7R)-3-hydroxy-7-prop-1-en-2-yl-5,6,7,8-tetrahydronaphthalene-1-carboxylate, respectively. These compounds all ultimately direct their activity to DNA polymerase iota. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Echitamidine influences DNA polymerase iota through a series of intermediate targets, possibly by modulating the activity of these intermediates. The shared involvement of DNA polymerase iota across different pathways underscores a possible role in the cellular response to these compounds, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
